From 5f13d67a50e6b0a44db60f96874d8a07e7276b1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DevWebeloper <gheith.sy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:21:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(stealth): align CPU sysctl, Metal GPU, and SMBIOS
 telemetry with MacBookPro16,1 spec

- Metal framework: support DARLING_METAL_GPU_NAME and DARLING_METAL_VRAM_MB to prevent host Vulkan device strings from leaking into Metal telemetry
- XNU emulation: implement binary integer sysctls for machdep.cpu.vendor (GenuineIntel), family, model, stepping, hw.product, hw.targettype, and kern.hv_vmm_present=0
- System profiler: emulate authentic dual GPU configuration (AMD Radeon Pro 5500M + Intel UHD Graphics 630)
- Process teardown: ignore zombie processes (State: Z) in process scanners, ensure robust cleanup of orphan darlingserver and Riot helpers
- Launchers: propagate DARLING_METAL_GPU_NAME and DARLING_METAL_VRAM_MB across launch-fork, run.sh, and run-riot-client; shield launch-upstream with redirection warning
- Tests: add coverage for launcher warnings, zombie process filtering, and Metal device telemetry
